<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matsudaira Katamori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1836–1893</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matsudaira Katamori was the last lord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> domain. In 1862 he became Protector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, policing the capital with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinsengumi">Shinsengumi</a> and supporting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Choshu</a> radicals. Branded an enemy of the court after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>, Aizu was besieged and defeated in 1868 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a>. He later served as chief priest of the Nikko Toshogu shrine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matsudaira-katamori.jpg" alt="Matsudaira Katamori" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matudaira_Katamori.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
